=== file: README.md ===
# Public Topic Research Brief

This on-demand Loom workflow screens a submitted subject before any external search. Sensitive or uncertain subjects end safely without research. A public subject is researched with a limit of three searches, reviewed by a critic, and revised by an editor into a concise one-page brief.

All agent instructions are stored in `prompts/`. The workflow has no human approval step and does not send or write anything.

## Run and check

From the project directory:

```text
weave check main.loom --no-env
weave test main.loom
weave run main.loom -w Main -i submitted_subject="public libraries"
```

The workflow uses the platform's available `gpt-6-luna` model and built-in web search. The budget caps a run at 12,000 tokens and six calls. Research and later-stage failures halt the run rather than returning an incomplete brief.
=== end ===

